.TH CONTENTS 5 "October 2026" "apkg 0.3.4" "Amix File Formats"
.SH NAME
contents \- the installed-software database
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /var/sadm/install/contents
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B contents
file lists every object installed packages own: one line per path name,
in sorted path name order.
.BR pkgadd (1M),
.BR installf (1M)
and
.BR removef (1M)
write it;
.BR pkgrm (1M),
.BR pkgchk (1M)
and
.BR pkginfo (1)
read it.  Edit it only with those tools.
.PP
Fields are separated by white space, and there is no quoting: a path name
cannot contain a space (the package tools refuse one).  A line starting
with
.B #
is a comment; the tools add one at the end saying when and by what the file
was last written.
.SH RECORDS
Every record starts with the path name and the file type, then the
installation class, then fields that depend on the type, and ends with
the names of the packages that own the object:
.PP
.nf
.ta 8n
f v e	path ftype class mode owner group size cksum modtime pkg...
d x p	path ftype class mode owner group pkg...
c b	path ftype class major minor mode owner group pkg...
s l	path=target ftype class pkg...
.fi
.TP 10
.I ftype
.B f
file,
.B e
file the administrator may edit,
.B v
file whose contents change (a log),
.B d
directory,
.B x
exclusive directory accessible only by this package,
.B p
named pipe,
.B c
and
.B b
character and block device,
.B s
symbolic link,
.B l
hard link
.TP
.I class
the installation class;
.B none
unless the package names one (see
.BR conffile (5))
.TP
.I mode
the permissions, in octal
.TP
.IR owner ", " group
by name
.TP
.IR size ", " cksum ", " modtime
the size in bytes, the
.BR sum (1)
checksum, and the modification time in seconds since 1970; for an
.B e
file installed by a class action script these describe the file as it is
on disk after the script
.TP
.I pkg
an owning package instance; several names mean the object is shared.  A
name may carry one status character in front:
.B +
ready for
.BR "installf \-f" ,
.B \-
ready for
.BR "removef \-f" ,
.B !
not found,
.B %
on a file server's read-only partition;
.B *
and
.B ~
are further states the tools accept.  A
.B ?
stands for a value the tool did not know.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
/etc/apkg.conf e conffile 0644 root sys 1521 51934 1793368699 APKG
/usr/apkg d none 0755 root sys APKG APKGENG
/usr/bin/apkg=/usr/apkg/bin/apkg s none APKG
/dev/console c none ? ? 0620 root tty core
.fi
.SH NOTES
The Amix 2.1 factory file holds a record for a file named
.B "TrueType Fonts"
and a repeated package name, which the stock tools cannot read;
.BR contents-fsck (1M)
finds and repairs such records.
.SH FILES
.TP 34
.B /var/sadm/install/contents
this file
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR contents-fsck (1M),
.BR pkgchk (1M),
.BR installf (1M),
.BR pkgmap (5),
.BR conffile (5)
